# agentsdk .env template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is git-ignored) and fill in the values you
# actually want to use. Anything exported in your shell still wins over the
# values here — viper's precedence is: explicit Set > flag > env > config
# (.env) > default, so a shell `export` overrides anything written below.
#
# .env is loaded by gosdk/config.Default() via spf13/viper (see
# gosdk/config/env.go). Anything that calls auth-cli must have already run
# gosdkconfig.Default(gosdkconfig.WithAppName(...)) before constructing an
# Antigravity authenticator.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Antigravity (Google installed-app OAuth2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required by: auth-cli login --provider antigravity_oauth
#
# viper keys (lowercased internally): antigravity_client_id,
# antigravity_client_secret. Bound to the env var names below in
# auth/provider/antigravity.init().
ANTIGRAVITY_CLIENT_ID=
ANTIGRAVITY_CLIENT_SECRET=